This test expects an `IllegalArgumentException` when passing `null` for publicId/systemId. However, the code only validates `name` with `Validate.notEmpty(name)`. There's no validation added for publicId or systemId being null. So this test would likely fail (no exception thrown), which would be a regression/bug introduced by this commit.

The test `constructorValidationThrowsExceptionOnNulls` expects an `IllegalArgumentException` when `publicId` and `systemId` are null, but the new code only added `Validate.notEmpty(name)` - there's no null validation for publicId or systemId. This test would fail, indicating a regression bug.

